If it was a gnome lord then I don't know, but if it was a
gnomish WIZARD that might explain things.
Messages like "You reel" or "Your brain is in fire" occur when you
get a spell cast upon you by a gnomish wizard or an orc or kobold
shaman. Since a gnomish wizard has some magic resistance, that would
also explain why your wand of cold didn't work.
And, since it is only a gnome, if you hit him with a longsword it is
quite conceivable you will kill him with only one or two hits.
As for weapons "bouncing off", I can't ever recall seeing that happen.
I have seen plenty of thrown weapons "miss" though, even against weak
monsters.

